# Core And Statarb Boundary

- Approved exception: `ADR 0005` (2026-11-04) authorizes moving the financial research kernel into `statarb/` and retaining `core/` names as compatibility facades. Do not restore the old close-array accounting or full-sample backtester.

- Treat `core/` as legacy research and prototype code. Preserve behavior, read it for reference, and keep changes there contained.
- Treat `statarb/` as the home for new platform-shell code: contracts-aligned runtime, adapters, control-plane modules, and future MVP packages.
- Do not place new `agent-operated` architecture into `core/`.
- Do not spread one new architectural slice across `core/` and `statarb/` unless the migration boundary and reason are documented.
- If a task implies moving responsibility from `core/` to `statarb/`, update the governance docs and ask for approval before proceeding.
